Reads the card from TEMPO/ when that folder exists, so one card can hold several
firmwares (chompi-sim's scripts/make-multi-card.py): the current directory is
changed after the mount and the Chromatic, Slice and Buffer folders are opened
relative to it. A card of TEMPO's own is unchanged: without the folder everything
stays in the root. Hardware builds take this patch as well (FatFs is built with
_FS_RPATH 2).

--- a/chompi_main.cpp
+++ b/chompi_main.cpp
@@ -384,6 +384,10 @@
     fsi.Init(FatFSInterface::Config::MEDIA_SD);
     System::Delay(100);
     f_mount(&fsi.GetSDFileSystem(), fsi.GetSDPath(), 1);
+    // On a card shared with other firmwares the sample folders and settings
+    // live in TEMPO/ (chompi-sim's scripts/make-multi-card.py); a card of
+    // TEMPO's own has no such folder and everything stays in the root.
+    f_chdir("/TEMPO");
 
     options.Init();
     tim_base_freq = System::GetPClk2Freq();
